course: dictionary
lesson: 1480
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The capital letter is a clue too. «CAFOD is the charity of the Catholic Church in England and Wales.» Here Catholic with a capital C is a name for a particular church.
explain: Now look at a small c. «Ella has catholic tastes in music.» There is no church in that sentence. Catholic with a small c is a formal word that means including many different kinds of things, so the sentence means her music taste is wide-ranging.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap it into the sentence: «Ella has wide-ranging tastes in music» still makes sense, so the small c meaning fits. Try a church meaning instead and the sentence falls apart.
fact: Catholic with a capital C means belonging to the Roman Catholic Church, the Christian church led by the Pope.
fact: A Catholic is a member of the Catholic Church.
fact: Catholic with a small c is formal and rare, and means including many different kinds of things.
fact: «The Pope is the Bishop of Rome and leader of the Catholic Church worldwide.»
fact: Many schools in Ireland, the UK, Australia, New Zealand, Canada and the USA are Catholic schools.
exercise: «CAFOD is the charity of the Catholic Church in England and Wales.» What does Catholic mean here? | A type of sports club | *Belonging to the Roman Catholic Church | Wide-ranging, including many different things | A big hall for school plays
exercise: Ella reads «catholic tastes in music» and thinks it is about a church. What does catholic mean here? | Belonging to the Pope | Very old and grey | A person who prays for the dead | *Including many different kinds of things
exercise: In «All Souls' Day, 2 November, is when Catholics and some Anglicans pray for the dead», find the word that means members of the Catholic Church. | November | Anglicans | Souls | *Catholics
test: «Catholic and Orthodox churches ordain only men.» In this sentence, ordain means: | *Make into priests | Sing loudly in a choir | Build with stone | Give away to charity
test: Which sentence uses catholic with a small c, meaning wide-ranging? | A Catholic is a member of that church | The Catholic school is down the road | *Her catholic tastes take in jazz, opera and rap | He prays at the Catholic church on Sundays
exam: «The Pope is the Bishop of Rome and leader of the Catholic Church worldwide.» Which meaning of Catholic fits here? | Very old and grey | Short and rude | Including many different kinds of things | *Belonging to the Roman Catholic Church
